sam: Quick heads-up — updating the Next.js starter to include a tiny auth-retry helper for client-side embeddings. Hit a race where token expired during concurrent requests.

tara: Can you paste the helper?

sam: Sure — located at /lib/withAuthRetry.ts\n\n```ts
let refreshPromise: Promise<void> | null = null;
export async function withAuthRetry(fn: () => Promise<any>) {
  try {
    return await fn();
  } catch (err) {
    if (err?.message === 'unauthorized') {
      if (!refreshPromise) refreshPromise = auth.refresh();
      await refreshPromise;
      refreshPromise = null;
      return await fn(); // replay once
    }
    throw err;
  }
}
```

sam: Tests added: embeds-queue.test simulates two concurrent calls where first triggers refresh, second awaits and succeeds. Kept demo retry policy minimal (1 replay + small backoff comment).

tara: Nice. Please add a short README blurb: prefer server-side embedding calls when possible; otherwise use withAuthRetry. Link to Optimize docs for production retry/backoff.

